+    "body": "Follow-up to PR https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2545 (review nit 1, review 5896585581).\n\n`hermes_cli/turn_session_activity.py` counts a TUI `core_update_pause` marker in `desktop/interrupted_turns.json` as `turn_live` using hard-coded 15 min / 2 attempts / enabled. `session_auto_continue` reads the configured `desktop.auto_continue.enabled`, `freshness_minutes`, `max_attempts`. With auto_continue disabled or lower bounds, a marker that will never continue reads live for up to 15 min.\n\nFix: read the same config (reuse session_auto_continue's loader) so the reader's bounds equal the producer's. Also fix the comment that says the gateway 1 h bound \"matches agent.gateway_auto_continue_freshness\" (it's the reader's own fail-closed cap) and move `import json` to module top in tests/hermes_cli/test_turn_session_activity.py.\n\nAcceptance: tests next to existing ones in tests/hermes_cli/test_turn_session_activity.py: disabled auto_continue \u2192 not live; freshness_minutes=5 with a 10-min-old marker \u2192 not live; max_attempts exhausted \u2192 not live; they fail on current main. Land via hermes-core-wt ship with independent exact-head review.",
